        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: High Bridge, Latah Creek, Spokane, Washington\n- Companies: Burlington Northern Railroad, Chicago Burlington & Quincy, Great Northern, Northern Pacific, Spokane Portland & Seattle\n- Events: Burlington Northern merger, High Bridge construction\n\nFacts:\n- Burlington Northern Railroad was created in 1970 through the merger of the Chicago, Burlington & Quincy, Great Northern, Northern Pacific, and Spokane, Portland & Seattle railways.\n- Burlington Northern Railroad operated from 1970 to 1996.\n- High Bridge is a railroad bridge over Latah Creek in Spokane, Washington.\n- High Bridge was constructed in 1972 by Burlington Northern Railroad.",
